WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.379 --> 00:00:02.970
-My first guest
has been nominated for

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:05.801
a Golden Globe, SAG Award,
and an Oscar

00:00:05.801 --> 00:00:08.567
for her work in the film
"Promising Young Woman,"

00:00:08.567 --> 00:00:12.100
which is in theaters
and on digital and DVD now.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.033
She's also hosting
"Saturday Night Live"

00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:16.400
this weekend,
with musical guest Kid Cudi.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.868
Please welcome Carey Mulligan!

00:00:18.868 --> 00:00:19.968
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:19.968 --> 00:00:21.467
-♪ Carey Mulligan,
Carey Mulligan,

00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:24.133
Carey Mulligan, y'all ♪

00:00:24.133 --> 00:00:25.734
♪ Lookin' promisin',
lookin' promisin',

00:00:25.734 --> 00:00:28.234
lookin' promisin', y'all ♪

00:00:28.234 --> 00:00:29.901
♪ Carey Mulligan,
Carey Mulligan,

00:00:29.901 --> 00:00:32.400
Carey Mulligan, y'all ♪

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:33.868
♪ Yeah ♪

00:00:33.868 --> 00:00:36.334
-Carey.
-Hi.

00:00:36.334 --> 00:00:38.801
-I'm so happy to see you.
Thank you for being on the show.

00:00:38.801 --> 00:00:41.334
-Thank you for having me.
It's so nice to be here.

00:00:41.334 --> 00:00:43.000
-Thank you for being here
in studio, too.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.400
-I know.
-With an audience.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:46.667
-It's my first one.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:48.367
-It feels great, right?
-So nice.

00:00:48.367 --> 00:00:50.767
-It just feels great,
the energy from that.

00:00:50.767 --> 00:00:51.968
Are you excited
about "Saturday Night Live"?

00:00:51.968 --> 00:00:52.968
Are you nervous?
How are you feeling?

00:00:52.968 --> 00:00:55.133
-Oh, my goodness.
I'm so excited.

00:00:55.133 --> 00:00:57.501
I'm very nervous.

00:00:57.501 --> 00:00:58.901
-Oh, don't be.

00:00:58.901 --> 00:01:01.434
-But it's going so quickly
in a way that I think is good.

00:01:01.434 --> 00:01:03.367
It's sort of like
you don't have time to think.

00:01:03.367 --> 00:01:06.300
You just go from
thing to thing to thing.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:07.667
-You've done
the writer's meeting,

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.000
where they all
pitch you ideas and --

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.968
-Yeah. And I hadn't
been around people

00:01:10.968 --> 00:01:15.167
for like a year and a half,
so I was just like everything --

00:01:15.167 --> 00:01:19.067
Every single pitch
was hilarious.

00:01:19.067 --> 00:01:21.567
I'm like, "God, this is
the funniest thing ever!"

00:01:21.567 --> 00:01:24.100
It was like,
I'm the best audience ever.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:28.601
'cause, you know, just human
proximity is so exciting.

00:01:28.601 --> 00:01:31.367
-I want to talk about
"Promising Young Woman."

00:01:31.367 --> 00:01:32.567
It came out earlier this year.
[ Light applause ]

00:01:32.567 --> 00:01:34.334
Sure, you can clap
if you feel like it. Sure.

00:01:34.334 --> 00:01:36.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:36.601 --> 00:01:39.334
Racking up the awards
ever since.

00:01:39.334 --> 00:01:40.567
Congratulations.

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:43.567
Best Actress nomination for
the Academy Award.

00:01:43.567 --> 00:01:45.601
That's your second one.
-Yeah.

00:01:45.601 --> 00:01:46.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:46.767 --> 00:01:49.267
What do you remember
about your first one?

00:01:49.267 --> 00:01:50.334
Do you remember?

00:01:50.334 --> 00:01:51.767
-I was talking about this
the other day

00:01:51.767 --> 00:01:55.000
to my friend, who was there,
and I -- My memory is so hazy.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:56.267
I don't remember --
I think I was just

00:01:56.267 --> 00:01:57.934
sort of so overwhelmed
by the whole thing.

00:01:57.934 --> 00:02:02.868
I just remember being in
a room with Sandra Bullock

00:02:02.868 --> 00:02:05.968
a lot and being like, "This is
the greatest moment of my life."

00:02:05.968 --> 00:02:07.434
I just --
-She's pretty cool.

00:02:07.434 --> 00:02:10.534
-Oh, man, she's so cool
and she's so gorgeous.

00:02:10.534 --> 00:02:13.501
And "Speed"
I've seen like 700 times.

00:02:13.501 --> 00:02:15.033
-"Speed"? Really?
-Oh, my goodness.

00:02:15.033 --> 00:02:16.267
"Speed" is the perfect film.

00:02:16.267 --> 00:02:18.634
"Speed" is the perfect film
in any situation.

00:02:18.634 --> 00:02:19.834
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:19.834 --> 00:02:21.067
-Really? If someone goes,
"Let's watch a movie,

00:02:21.067 --> 00:02:22.501
what do we watch?", you go --

00:02:22.501 --> 00:02:25.601
-Oh, you could be in any mood,
and you'd be like, "Speed."

00:02:25.601 --> 00:02:27.267
There's never a time
not to watch "Speed."

00:02:27.267 --> 00:02:30.734
-I watched this
and I was watching it

00:02:30.734 --> 00:02:31.734
and I go, "Oh, no, no, no.

00:02:31.734 --> 00:02:33.067
This is terrible."

00:02:33.067 --> 00:02:35.701
And I just felt -- I mean,
the movie is not terrible.

00:02:35.701 --> 00:02:37.367
-Okay.
-The situation was terrible.

00:02:37.367 --> 00:02:39.400
-Yes.
-Sorry. The movie is fantastic.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:40.434
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:40.434 --> 00:02:41.467
Oh, my gosh.
-Start again.

00:02:41.467 --> 00:02:42.467
-That's why
I don't review movies.

00:02:42.467 --> 00:02:43.467
-Yeah.

00:02:43.467 --> 00:02:45.234
-No, I was saying the situation.

00:02:45.234 --> 00:02:46.934
I go -- I felt bad for you,
your character.

00:02:46.934 --> 00:02:48.200
And I go, "Oh, no, no, no.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:50.267
I don't like
where this is going to go."

00:02:50.267 --> 00:02:53.501
Then...
Wow! Whoa!

00:02:53.501 --> 00:02:55.000
If you haven't seen it. Wow!

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:56.601
And I was like,
"That right there."

00:02:56.601 --> 00:02:58.534
Vote -- Anything I can do.

00:02:58.534 --> 00:03:00.200
Whatever I can do
to tell you that

00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:01.467
you are phenomenal.

00:03:01.467 --> 00:03:04.000
That was such a good...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:06.868
And the whole thing
played out great.

00:03:06.868 --> 00:03:10.667
It is a -- It touches on
a rough subject,

00:03:10.667 --> 00:03:13.868
but, in a weird way, there is
comedy in there, as well.

00:03:13.868 --> 00:03:15.834
Bo Burnham was hilariously funny
in it, I thought.

00:03:15.834 --> 00:03:18.167
-He's so brilliant, Bo, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:20.767
And we've got -- I mean, that's
the thing about the film is,

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:22.467
it is tackling
a difficult subject,

00:03:22.467 --> 00:03:23.901
but it's definitely --

00:03:23.901 --> 00:03:25.901
I mean, the majority of the cast
were all comedians.

00:03:25.901 --> 00:03:27.767
There's Jennifer Coolidge.

00:03:27.767 --> 00:03:29.334
-Jennifer Coolidge,
by the way, is --

00:03:29.334 --> 00:03:31.300
-Genius.
-She's unbelievable.

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:32.767
-Yeah.
-I mean, she plays your mom.

00:03:32.767 --> 00:03:34.400
-Yeah.
-Would she improvise at all?

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:35.801
-Oh, my goodness.

00:03:35.801 --> 00:03:39.033
Jennifer was -- So, she was kind
of -- We were on a 23-day shoot,

00:03:39.033 --> 00:03:40.267
so it was very quick.

00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:42.434
So there wasn't much time
to sort of mess around.

00:03:42.434 --> 00:03:44.467
But there was
a dinner-table scene

00:03:44.467 --> 00:03:47.033
in the movie where Bo,
who is my boyfriend,

00:03:47.033 --> 00:03:48.067
comes and meets my parents.

00:03:48.067 --> 00:03:50.467
And Emerald Fennell,
our director,

00:03:50.467 --> 00:03:52.434
came in at the beginning and
said, "Just sort of, like --

00:03:52.434 --> 00:03:54.667
You know, just, like,
have, like, small talk.

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:56.534
Like, you know, ask her what
she does for a living,

00:03:56.534 --> 00:03:57.701
blah blah blah."

00:03:57.701 --> 00:03:59.267
So, we're sitting there,
and Bo's like, "So --

00:03:59.267 --> 00:04:00.334
Oh, this is delicious.

00:04:00.334 --> 00:04:01.667
What do you do for a living?"

00:04:01.667 --> 00:04:04.868
And Jennifer's first answer was,
"Well, I've discovered,

00:04:04.868 --> 00:04:06.901
late in life,
that I've got a real talent

00:04:06.901 --> 00:04:08.667
for fish-tank interior design."

00:04:08.667 --> 00:04:10.901
-[ Laughs ] What?

00:04:10.901 --> 00:04:13.133
-But it just, like,
ruined everyone.

00:04:13.133 --> 00:04:14.968
And, so, then we --
And I can't --

00:04:14.968 --> 00:04:16.834
You know, I'm the
worst person in the world

00:04:16.834 --> 00:04:18.300
for this, and so I just lost it.

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:21.334
And then we started again
and we got to the same point.

00:04:21.334 --> 00:04:23.067
"So, what do you do
for a living?"

00:04:23.067 --> 00:04:27.567
"Well, I train small animals to
detect carbon monoxide."

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:29.367
You know?
And it kept on and on like this.

00:04:29.367 --> 00:04:30.400
-How do you think of that?

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:32.467
-It got to the point
where I was --

00:04:32.467 --> 00:04:34.334
Actually, in the film,
there is a tiny bit

00:04:34.334 --> 00:04:35.667
where you can see that I've
just completely lost it.

00:04:35.667 --> 00:04:37.367
And Emerald, I think,
probably ran out of time.

00:04:37.367 --> 00:04:38.667
She was like, "That will do."

00:04:38.667 --> 00:04:39.834
-You're like,
"Just take me off set.

00:04:39.834 --> 00:04:41.634
Just get me --
I don't want to be rude,

00:04:41.634 --> 00:04:43.133
but get me out of this set."

00:04:43.133 --> 00:04:46.100
I've been -- Yeah, I've been in
that situation many times.

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:48.334
But I love
the attention to detail

00:04:48.334 --> 00:04:49.601
and little details.

00:04:49.601 --> 00:04:53.000
And one thing I've noticed,
I loved your nails.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.467
-Thank you.

00:04:54.467 --> 00:04:57.200
-They're multicolored.
See these nails?

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:59.367
And I just --
I kept looking at them

00:04:59.367 --> 00:05:01.300
and I go, "Oh, my gosh."

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:02.667
It was just part of
your character

00:05:02.667 --> 00:05:04.133
and part of the movie
for me now.

00:05:04.133 --> 00:05:06.167
And then we were
talking backstage.

00:05:06.167 --> 00:05:09.567
I was like, "Are you going to go
to the Oscars with your mom?"

00:05:09.567 --> 00:05:10.968
-Mm-hmm.
-And no, not this year.

00:05:10.968 --> 00:05:12.400
-Well, no.

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:15.467
Mum came with me last time,
and, actually, she's amazing.

00:05:15.467 --> 00:05:16.868
She always comes with me
when I'm traveling,

00:05:16.868 --> 00:05:18.400
especially with my children.

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:19.634
But because of the situation
at the moment,

00:05:19.634 --> 00:05:21.133
she couldn't get in.

00:05:21.133 --> 00:05:25.100
But she grabbed me
right before I left the airport

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:27.934
and she was like, "I have a
thing for you, for the Oscars."

00:05:27.934 --> 00:05:29.834
She always gives me these, like,
sentimental presents

00:05:29.834 --> 00:05:32.367
you know, to open, like,
on important days.

00:05:32.367 --> 00:05:34.868
She was like, "But you should
just have it now,

00:05:34.868 --> 00:05:35.868
but it's a bit weird.

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:37.033
But, you know,
just have it now."

00:05:37.033 --> 00:05:38.567
And I was like, "Okay, mum."

00:05:38.567 --> 00:05:43.033
And she gave me this box,
and within the box was a box.

00:05:43.033 --> 00:05:46.667
-Wait a second. In trolls or --

00:05:46.667 --> 00:05:49.267
-No, she gives me this box,
and I open --

00:05:49.267 --> 00:05:50.934
Well, I mean, do you want to --
-You brought it here.

00:05:50.934 --> 00:05:52.434
-Yeah, I brought it.

00:05:52.434 --> 00:05:55.367
I brought it all the way -- It
came all the way from England.

00:05:57.534 --> 00:06:01.267
-That's the nails.
Where did your mom get them?

00:06:01.267 --> 00:06:03.868
-So, the last day of filming,
I guess.

00:06:03.868 --> 00:06:04.968
I came home and I was, like,

00:06:04.968 --> 00:06:06.534
watching
"America's Ninja Warrior"

00:06:06.534 --> 00:06:08.267
and I was on the sofa
and I just sort of started

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:10.400
ripping them off, because they
had been really annoying.

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:12.634
And I just -- I don't know --

00:06:12.634 --> 00:06:14.801
left them on the side of
the sofa or something.

00:06:14.801 --> 00:06:18.801
And my mom was like, "Ooh, I'm
going to squirrel these away."

00:06:18.801 --> 00:06:21.567
-Normally, if I see a box of
nails in someone's apartment,

00:06:21.567 --> 00:06:23.300
I'm like, "Call 911."

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:26.701
Yeah, or at least dial 9-1
and hope for the best.

00:06:26.701 --> 00:06:28.334
But this is pretty kind of cool.

00:06:28.334 --> 00:06:30.100
-Yeah. And then
she found this, like,

00:06:30.100 --> 00:06:32.634
weird, creepy box,
and, you know...

00:06:32.634 --> 00:06:35.300
-Yeah, with a nice light in it.
I think it's fanta--

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:36.934
-Yeah.
-I love it, by the way.

00:06:36.934 --> 00:06:38.000
-Yeah, no, me too.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:39.734
-Mom,
that's very, very thoughtful.

00:06:39.734 --> 00:06:40.801
It's very, very cool.

00:06:40.801 --> 00:06:42.701
And I love that
you brought it with you.

00:06:42.701 --> 00:06:44.200
-It's coming to
the Oscars with me.

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:45.400
-Is that right?
-No, it's not really.

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:46.400
I probably won't be able to
fit it in my bag.

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:47.701
-Yeah, I think you should do it.

00:06:47.701 --> 00:06:49.467
No, we all think
you should do it.

00:06:49.467 --> 00:06:51.501
Yeah, you have to.

00:06:51.501 --> 00:06:53.100
Thank you again for coming
to our show.

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:54.467
I appreciate it. Break a leg.

00:06:54.467 --> 00:06:56.501
Everybody heard that
you're a joy to work with,

00:06:56.501 --> 00:06:57.501
so everyone's excited.

00:06:57.501 --> 00:06:58.634
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:58.634 --> 00:07:00.901
Here's Carey Mulligan in
"Promising Young Woman."

00:07:00.901 --> 00:07:02.234
Take a look at this.

00:07:02.234 --> 00:07:03.601
-I think you should go.

00:07:03.601 --> 00:07:06.467
-But a second ago, you were
determined for me to stay.

00:07:06.467 --> 00:07:09.067
You were pretty insistent,
actually.

00:07:09.067 --> 00:07:11.334
-I'm a nice guy.

00:07:11.334 --> 00:07:12.934
-Are you?

00:07:12.934 --> 00:07:14.767
-I thought we had
a connection, I guess.

00:07:14.767 --> 00:07:16.334
-A connection?

00:07:16.334 --> 00:07:19.467
Okay.

00:07:19.467 --> 00:07:20.534
What do I do for a living?

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:24.267
Sorry.
Maybe that one is too hard.

00:07:24.267 --> 00:07:26.868
How old am I?

00:07:26.868 --> 00:07:30.934
How long have I lived
in the city?

00:07:30.934 --> 00:07:32.667
What are my hobbies?

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:37.501
What's my name?

